#!/usr/bin/python3
"""
firox-explorer: Firox Explorer, the Firox file manager (it opens folders
everywhere: /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list; also /usr/bin/firox-explorer).

    firox-explorer [FOLDER|URI]     open a window there (default: Home)
    firox-explorer --find [FOLDER]  open it ready to search FOLDER and all
                                    its subfolders (Start > Search)
    firox-explorer --connect        open it with Connect to Server
    firox-explorer --connect-saved  connect the connections marked "Connect
                                    when I log in", then exit (run at login)
    firox-explorer --test NAME      check a saved connection step by step and
                                    write a report (secrets blanked) to
                                    ~/.local/state/firox/mounts/ID-test.log

Tabs (Ctrl+T, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab, Alt+1..9; middle-click a folder or a
sidebar place to open it in a new tab; drop files on a tab to put them in
its folder): each tab has its own folder, history, views and search (class
Tab; Explorer's per-tab attributes forward to the current tab).

Browse your files, drives and network places; Icons or Details view; Back,
Forward, Up, an address bar and filtering as you type in the search box
(with "Subfolders" on, it searches every folder inside too).
Cut, Copy, Paste (shared with the desktop), Rename, New Folder, Move to
Recycle Bin, Delete, Properties, Open With, drag and drop, and Restore /
Empty in the Recycle Bin.

A menu bar (File, Edit, View, Go, Bookmarks, Tools, Help): sort by name,
size, type or date; select none / invert; copy location; new text document;
bookmarks shared with GTK's file dialogs (~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks) and
shown in the sidebar; Options and Keyboard Shortcuts. View settings are kept
in ~/.config/firox/explorer.conf.

Connect to Server mounts Windows shares, SFTP, FTP, WebDAV, Amazon S3 (and
S3-compatible storage such as Wasabi, R2 or MinIO) and Backblaze B2 in your
session only, with passwords in your login keyring (see firox_mounts).
"""

